.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/benchmark/reports/compiled-routing/2026-07-21--real--luna-high/skill-benchmark-report.json:29:        "stderr": "OpenAI Codex v0.144.4\n--------\nworkdir: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover\nmodel: gpt-5.6-luna\nprovider: openai\napproval: never\nsandbox: read-only\nreasoning effort: high\nreasoning summaries: none\nsession id: 019f83a2-2f88-7d92-a701-956e20c79296\n--------\nuser\nYou are analyzing skill routing only - do NOT edit files.\nTask: Use deep research to investigate why our advisor sometimes routes iterative investigation prompts incorrectly, and write the findings as a research summary.\n\nWithin the `system-deep-loop` skill ONLY (do not route to or read any other skill), consulting that skill's SKILL.md router, determine: (1) the detected SURFACE if the skill defines one (e.g. WEBFLOW / OPENCODE), else \"UNKNOWN\", (2) the sub-language if any, else \"none\", (3) the exact reference/asset file paths you would load (relative to the skill root, e.g. references/... and assets/...), (4) the agent you would dispatch, or \"none\".\nAs the FIRST line of your answer, emit this exact declaration shape:\nROUTED: {\"workflowMode\": \"<mode>\", \"intents\": [\"<mode>\", \"...\"]}\nThen emit ONLY a fenced ```json code block, nothing after it:\n{\"surface\": \"...\", \"subLanguage\": \"...\", \"resources\": [\"references/...\"], \"assets\": [\"assets/...\"], \"agent\": \"none\", \"disambiguation\": false}\nhook: SessionStart\nhook: SessionStart\nhook: SessionStart\nhook: SessionStart\nhook: SessionStart\nhook: SessionStart\nhook: SessionStart\nhook: SessionStart\nhook: SessionStart Completed\nhook: SessionStart Completed\nhook: SessionStart Completed\nhook: SessionStart Completed\nhook: SessionStart Completed\nhook: SessionStart Completed\nhook: SessionStart Completed\nhook: SessionStart Completed\nhook: UserPromptSubmit\nhook: UserPromptSubmit\nhook: UserPromptSubmit\nhook: UserPromptSubmit\nhook: UserPromptSubmit Completed\nhook: UserPromptSubmit Completed\nhook: UserPromptSubmit Completed\nhook: UserPromptSubmit Completed\ncodex\nRouting-only analysis. I’ll inspect the `system-deep-loop` router and load no other skill.\nhook: PreToolUse\nhook: PreToolUse\nhook: PreToolUse Completed\nhook: PreToolUse Completed\nmcp: system-spec-memory/memory_match_triggers started\nmcp: system-spec-memory/memory_match_triggers (failed)\nuser cancelled MCP tool call\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md\" in /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover\n succeeded in 0ms:\n---\nname: system-deep-loop\nversion: 2.0.0.0\ndescription: \"Routes research, review, AI Council, improvement, and named-standard alignment modes through registry-selected packets.\"\nallowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task, WebFetch]\n---\n\n<!-- Keywords: system-deep-loop, deep-loop, deep-research, deep-review, deep-ai-council, deep-improvement, deep-alignment, alignment, conformance, standard-authority, alignment-lane, conformance-review, read-only-default, context-gathering, reuse-catalog, autoresearch, iterative-research, review-loop, deep-review-wave, release-readiness, severity-findings, P0-P1-P2, ai-council, council-deliberation, multi-seat-planning, agent-improvement, benchmark-harness, model-benchmark, skill-benchmark, convergence-detection, externalized-state, coverage-graph, mode-registry, workflowmode, runtimeloop-type, backendkind -->\n\n# System Deep Loop\n\nOne skill, five active workflow families, one nested runtime layer. `system-deep-loop` is the public, advisor-routable home for active deep-loop personas; `runtime/` is the frozen, MCP-free infrastructure layer it consumes (formerly the separate `deep-loop-runtime` skill, merged into this hub 2026-07-08). This hub holds NO per-mode convergence, state, or synthesis logic — each active mode keeps its own contract in its packet, and the hub only routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`.\n\nUse `@context` for one-shot retrieval, `/deep:research` for iterative investigation with a bounded context snapshot, `/deep:review` for iterative audit with a bounded review snapshot, `/deep:alignment` for read-only-by-default conformance against a named standard authority, or `/speckit:plan` for implementation planning.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\nUse this skill (through the hub) for any active deep-loop workflow. Invoke it as `Skill(system-deep-loop)` (optionally with a mode hint such as `research: <request>` or `alignment: <request>`); the hub classifies the request, resolves a `workflowMode`, and loads the matching nested mode packet. Active `/deep:*` commands and native agent types remain as complementary surfaces over the same packets.\n\n| Mode | Use it for | Packet | Command | Agent |\n|------|-----------|--------|---------|-------|\n| **research** | Outward, web + code iterative investigation → `research/research.md` | `system-deep-loop/deep-research/` | `/deep:research` | `deep-research` |\n| **review** | Iterative review loop → P0/P1/P2 findings + verdict | `system-deep-loop/deep-review/` | `/deep:review` | `deep-review` |\n| **ai-council** | Multi-seat planning deliberation → `ai-council/**` artifacts | `system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/` | `/deep:ai-council` | `ai-council` |\n| **improvement** (3 lanes) | Evaluator-first improvement: `agent-improvement`, `model-benchmark`, `skill-benchmark` | `system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/` | `/deep:agent-improvement` · `/deep:model-benchmark` · `/deep:skill-benchmark` | `deep-improvement` |\n| **alignment** | Read-only-by-default conformance audit against a named standard authority | `system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/` | `/deep:alignment` | `deep-alignment` |\n\n### When NOT to Use\n- A single quick read/edit (no loop) — use the relevant code or doc skill directly.\n- Backend/runtime support (executor, coverage-graph, scoring, fan-out) — that is `runtime/`, consumed here, not invoked as a user workflow (formerly the separate deep-loop-runtime skill).\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\nRouting is **registry-driven** (invokable-hub, Option E). `mode-registry.json` is the single source of truth; the hub reads it and does not re-derive the mapping. When invoked as `Skill(system-deep-loop[, \"<mode>: <request>\"])`, the hub classifies the request to a `workflowMode`, resolves it through the registry, and loads `registry[mode].packet`. The advisor routes any deep-loop query to the single identity `system-deep-loop`; the hub then picks the mode. The `/deep:*` commands and native agent types remain as complementary surfaces — they reach the same packets through static routers/agent definitions — and the hub holds NO per-mode logic.\n\n> **Compiled routing (opt-in, flag-gated, additive).** When `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=1`, resolve the mode via the compiled router contract first:\n> ```bash\n> node .opencode/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub system-deep-loop --prompt \"<task>\"\n> ```\n> Follow the returned decision — `route` (use its `targets`), `clarify`/`defer` (disambiguate), `reject` (refuse). On a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel or any error, use the routing below. The front door self-gates on serving-authority, and the flag is **off by default**, so this is inert until compiled routing is activated for `system-deep-loop`.\n\nThis hub is an intent/registry router, not a keyed resource-discovery router: at runtime it omits `discover_markdown_resources` and only guards registry-selected packet loads, never selecting hub-level `references/<key>/` or `assets/<key>/` resources by runtime key. It does carry a second-layer surface router at `shared/references/smart-routing.md` — a benchmark/replay artifact (mirroring sk-prompt/sk-code) that maps a resolved mode's intent to packet-qualified child leaves so router-replay can emit canonical `{workflowMode, leafResourceId}` typed pairs against `leaf-manifest.json`. That surface layer never re-decides the mode and is not a runtime hub discovery surface; the hub still routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json` alone.\n\n### Note on the frontmatter `allowed-tools` grant\n\nThe hub's own routing logic is read-only (classify, guard a path, load a packet). The frontmatter `allowed-tools` list is nonetheless broad because, per the two-axis hub canon contract, a hub's tool grant MUST equal the exact union of every registered mode's `toolSurface.allowed` in `mode-registry.json` — not the tool set the hub's own logic uses. This is a hard invariant enforced by `parent-skill-check.cjs` (check 3j: \"hub allowed-tools equals the union of mode tool surfaces\"); narrowing the frontmatter grant to only what routing-only logic needs would fail that check and break every mode whose `toolSurface` isn't a subset of the narrowed list. Treat the breadth of `allowed-tools` as evidence of the child modes' combined needs, not of mutating logic living in the hub.\n\n### The three-tier discriminator\n- **`workflowMode`** — the public active mode key: `research`, `review`, `ai-council`, `alignment`, and the three improvement lanes `agent-improvement`, `model-benchmark`, `skill-benchmark`.\n- **`runtimeLoopType`** — the graph-backed convergence key consumed by `runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs` (validated against active `research|review|council`). **Explicit `null` for all three improvement lanes; never inferred from `workflowMode`.** Note `ai-council` maps to `runtimeLoopType: council`, while `alignment` maps to `runtimeLoopType: review`.\n- **`backendKind`** — which backend runs the mode: `runtime-loop-type` (research/review/ai-council/alignment) or `improvement-host` (`deep-improvement/scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode`).\n\n### Routing rule\n```\nclassify the request to a workflowMode (dominant deep-loop intent; mode hint like \"research: ...\" overrides)\nguard mode-registry.json inside SKILL_ROOT and read it as data\nif classifier confidence is low or no mode dominates:\n  → return UNKNOWN_FALLBACK with a disambiguation checklist: choose research, review, ai-council, alignment, or one improvement lane\nelse:\n  → resolve workflowMode from the hint / classified intent (or the /deep:* command / advisor alias)\n  → find registry[mode]; if missing, return UNKNOWN_FALLBACK instead of loading a guessed path\n  → guard registry[mode].packet/SKILL.md inside SKILL_ROOT and load it only if the packet directory and SKILL.md both exist\n       e.g. registry[\"research\"].packet → system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md\n       e.g. registry[\"alignment\"].packet → system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/SKILL.md\n       (the 3 improvement modes all share the system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/ packet)\n  → if registry[mode].runtimeLoopType !== null: backend = convergence.cjs --loop-type <runtimeLoopType>\n     else: backend = improvement loop-host (--mode), per backendKind\n```\n\nRouter-driven loads MUST use `_guard_in_skill(relative_path)` before `load()`, reject paths that escape this skill or do not end in `.md`, and check `if packet_base.exists()` plus `if packet_skill.exists()` before loading. The fallback must name the unresolved `workflowMode` when known, avoid loading any guessed packet, and ask the operator to provide one of the registered modes or the matching `/deep:*` command.\n\nIntent classification favors the single dominant active deep-loop mode; a mode hint (`research: ...`, `review: ...`, `ai-council: ...`, `alignment: ...`, or an improvement lane) overrides the classifier. The legacy advisor projection maps stay hardcoded and drift-guarded against the registry, and the command files remain static routers with hardcoded asset/mode routing; neither resolves from `mode-registry.json` at runtime, but both stay equal to its projection.\n\nPer-mode behavior is **not flattened**: each active packet keeps its own convergence math, state shape, artifacts, and tool-permission guards (research has WebFetch; review/ai-council are code/inward-only; alignment is a named-standard, read-only-by-default conformance audit; improvement is the only direct mutation family). Exactly one `graph-metadata.json` — this hub's — is preserved, so the advisor discovers exactly one skill identity regardless of which surface (hub `Skill()`, `/deep:*` command, or agent) reaches a mode.\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Layout\n```\nsystem-deep-loop/\n  SKILL.md               # this routing hub (no per-mode logic)\n  mode-registry.json     # the three-tier discriminator + advisorRouting (single source of truth)\n  graph-metadata.json    # the ONE advisor identity for the whole skill\n  deep-research/   deep-review/   deep-ai-council/   deep-improvement/   deep-alignment/   # active mode packets\n  shared/synthesis/      # workflows-shared synthesis (e.g. emitResourceMap)\n```\n\nEach active mode packet keeps its own `SKILL.md`, `references/`, `scripts/`, `assets/`, `feature-catalog/`, or `manual-testing-playbook/` as applicable, with internal paths repointed and **no per-packet `graph-metadata.json`** — only this hub carries one, so the advisor discovers exactly one skill. The `deep-ai-council` packet folder follows the standard `folder == packetSkillName` convention (`deep-ai-council`); its legacy public surfaces (the `/deep:ai-council` command and the `ai-council` agent) intentionally keep the shorter `ai-council` key, so always resolve the packet path through `mode-registry.json` rather than hardcoding it.\n\n### Backend\nAll modes consume `runtime/` (frozen, MCP-free): executor config, prompt-pack, validation, atomic state, coverage-graph, Bayesian scoring, fan-out, the council primitives, and the promoted plumbing (capability resolver, artifact-root, loop-lock CLI, lifecycle taxonomy). The runtime never gains an `improvement` loopType — improvement stays host-driven.\n\n---\n\n## 4. RULES\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS\n- **ALWAYS** resolve a mode through `mode-registry.json` (read the `packet` key; never hardcode a router mapping or packet path in the hub).\n- **ALWAYS** keep advisor projection maps hardcoded and drift-guarded against the registry; command mode routing is still hardcoded in the command files and does not resolve through `mode-registry.json`.\n- **ALWAYS** keep each mode's convergence/state/artifact contract in its packet — the hub stays logic-free.\n- **ALWAYS** keep exactly one `graph-metadata.json` (this hub's) so the advisor sees one skill identity, whether a mode is reached via `Skill(system-deep-loop)`, a `/deep:*` command, or an agent.\n- **ALWAYS** keep `Skill(system-deep-loop)` hub routing, the `/deep:*` commands, and the agent types as complementary surfaces over the same packets — never let one surface fork per-mode logic out of its packet.\n\n### ⛔ NEVER\n- **NEVER** add an `improvement` `loopType` to `runtime/convergence.cjs` (improvement is host-driven; `runtimeLoopType` stays `null`).\n- **NEVER** infer `runtimeLoopType` from `workflowMode` — read it from the registry (explicit `null` is load-bearing).\n- **NEVER** let a read-only mode (research/review/ai-council/alignment) reach the improvement mutation scripts (`promote-candidate.cjs`/`rollback-candidate.cjs`).\n- **NEVER** add a `graph-metadata.json` or a discoverable skill marker inside a mode packet or `shared/`.\n\n### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n- A new mode is needed beyond the seven registered — extend `mode-registry.json` and open a packet, do not bolt logic onto the hub.\n- A change would require the runtime to gain MCP tools or an improvement loopType — that contradicts the architecture; escalate.\n\n---\n\n## 5. REFERENCES\n\n- Backend: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/` (frozen, consumed by every mode; nested infrastructure, not a separate skill).\n- Mode packets: `deep-research/SKILL.md`, `deep-review/SKILL.md`, `deep-ai-council/SKILL.md`, `deep-improvement/SKILL.md`, `deep-alignment/SKILL.md` (per-mode detail).\n- Commands: the active `/deep:*` commands under `.opencode/commands/deep/` (complementary surface).\n- Registry: `mode-registry.json` (the routing contract — the authoritative `packet` paths).\n\n---\n\n## 6. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- The hub resolves one primary active `workflowMode` for the request through `mode-registry.json` (improvement folds to the right lane via the registry, never by array order).\n- The selected mode packet owns the detailed convergence/state/artifact workflow; the hub stayed routing-only.\n- `Skill(system-deep-loop[, hint])` reaches a mode, and the `/deep:*` commands and agent types still reach the same packets.\n- Exactly one `graph-metadata.json` exists for the whole skill; no packet carries its own.\n\n---\n\n## 7. INTEGRATION POINTS\n\n### Modes\n- `research` — outward web + code iterative investigation (`research/research.md`).\n- `review` — iterative review loop, P0/P1/P2 findings + verdict.\n- `ai-council` — multi-seat planning deliberation (`ai-council/**` artifacts).\n- `improvement` (3 lanes) — evaluator-first agent/model/skill improvement.\n- `alignment` — read-only-by-default conformance audit against a named standard authority (`alignment/` artifacts).\n\n### Surfaces and Consumers\n- `Skill(system-deep-loop)` is the invokable hub; active `/deep:*` commands and the agent types (`deep-research`, `deep-review`, `ai-council`, `deep-improvement`, `deep-alignment`) are complementary surfaces over the same packets.\n- `runtime/` is the frozen, MCP-free backend every mode consumes (nested infrastructure, not a separate skill).\n- `/speckit:plan` consumes `@context` packages plus research/review/alignment outputs; spec-folder docs consume research/review/alignment output.\n\n---\n\n## 8. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- Pattern: `.opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md` (parent-skill hub + nested packets, the one-graph-metadata invariant).\n- Sibling example: `.opencode/skills/sk-design/` (the same invokable-hub + `mode-registry.json` Option E pattern).\n- Registry: `mode-registry.json` (this hub's routing contract).\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json && sed -n '1,300p' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md\" in /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover\n succeeded in 0ms:\n{\n  \"skill\": \"system-deep-loop\",\n  \"version\": \"2.0.0.1\",\n  \"resourceContractVersion\": 1,\n  \"description\": \"Declarative mode registry: the single source of truth for the three-tier discriminator (workflowMode/runtimeLoopType/backendKind) PLUS the advisorRouting projection. The advisor keeps its hardcoded projection maps (Python DEEP_ROUTING_MODE_BY_KEY, TypeScript DEEP_MODE_BY_CANONICAL) in sync with this registry via a CI drift-guard test (maps == registry projection); the advisor does NOT read this file at runtime, which avoids cross-skill import coupling on the advisor hot path.\",\n  \"discriminator\": {\n    \"workflowMode\": \"Public command/advisor/mode key. Stable identity used in commands, advisor aliases, and this registry. Carried by every mode.\",\n    \"runtimeLoopType\": \"The graph-backed convergence loop key consumed by runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs. Validated against exactly research|review|council. Explicit null for improvement-host modes; NEVER inferred from workflowMode.\",\n    \"backendKind\": \"Which backend actually runs the mode: runtime-loop-type (runtime/ convergence) or improvement-host (deep-improvement/scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode).\"\n  },\n  \"advisorRoutingContract\": {\n    \"routingClass\": \"How the advisor finds the mode. 'lexical' = weighted-regex scoring in skill_advisor.py AND present in both projection maps. 'alias-fold' = TS DEEP_MODE_BY_CANONICAL only (alias projection, not lexically scored). 'metadata' = resolved by skill membership; no advisor map entry. 'command-bridge' = routed by its /deep:* command, not an advisor map entry.\",\n    \"legacyAdvisorId\": \"The legacy deep-* skill id the projection maps key on (present for lexical + alias-fold modes only).\",\n    \"advisorDefaultMode\": \"Marks the default mode a multi-mode legacy id folds to (deep-improvement -> agent-improvement). Never inferred from array order.\",\n    \"legacyAliases\": \"The TypeScript scorer alias set (aliases.ts SKILL_ALIAS_GROUPS[legacyAdvisorId]) the merged-identity layer keys on; the drift-guard asserts these match it order-insensitive. The Python deep-router uses its own alias set + regex patterns by design (same keys, different values), so the guard only cross-checks that each legacyAdvisorId key also exists in the Python SKILL_ALIAS_GROUPS.\",\n    \"packetSkillName\": \"The packet's SKILL.md name. Most packets use folder == packetSkillName == deep-<mode> (e.g. deep-ai-council). Exception: the three improvement lanes (agent/skill/model) multiplex onto one shared packet 'deep-improvement', so several workflowModes map to that single folder/packetSkillName. The legacy public key 'ai-council' is preserved only on the command/agent surfaces, not on the packet folder/name.\",\n    \"driftGuard\": \".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/routing-registry-drift-guard.vitest.ts\"\n  },\n  \"extensions\": {\n    \"runtime-loop\": {\n      \"description\": \"Declares the runtime-loop backend: modes with backendKind 'runtime-loop-type' converge over runtime/, keyed by runtimeLoopType (research|review|council). runtimeLoopType is explicit null for improvement-host modes and is never inferred from workflowMode.\",\n      \"runtimeLoopTypes\": [\"research\", \"review\", \"council\"]\n    },\n    \"advisor-projection\": {\n      \"description\": \"Declares that the advisor keeps hardcoded projection maps (Python DEEP_ROUTING_MODE_BY_KEY, TypeScript DEEP_MODE_BY_CANONICAL) in sync with this registry's advisorRouting projection. The advisor does not read this file at runtime; a CI drift-guard asserts maps == registry projection.\",\n      \"driftGuard\": \".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/routing-registry-drift-guard.vitest.ts\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"deprecatedModes\": [],\n  \"modes\": [\n    {\n      \"workflowMode\": \"research\",\n      \"runtimeLoopType\": \"research\",\n      \"backendKind\": \"runtime-loop-type\",\n      \"packetKind\": \"workflow\",\n      \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": false,\n      \"toolSurface\": {\n        \"allowed\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Edit\", \"Bash\", \"Grep\", \"Glob\", \"Task\", \"WebFetch\"],\n        \"forbidden\": [],\n        \"mutatesWorkspace\": true,\n        \"bashAllowlist\": []\n      },\n      \"packet\": \"deep-research\",\n      \"command\": \"/deep:research\",\n      \"agent\": \"deep-research\",\n      \"artifactRoot\": \"research/\",\n      \"aliases\": [\"deep-research\", \"research loop\", \"iterative investigation workflow\", \"research convergence detection\", \"autoresearch\", \"iterative-research\"],\n      \"advisorRouting\": {\n        \"routingClass\": \"lexical\",\n        \"legacyAdvisorId\": \"deep-research\",\n        \"legacyAliases\": [\"command-spec-kit-deep-research\", \"/deep:research\", \"spec_kit:deep-research\", \"deep-research\", \"sk-deep-research\"],\n        \"packetSkillName\": \"deep-research\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"workflowMode\": \"review\",\n      \"runtimeLoopType\": \"review\",\n      \"backendKind\": \"runtime-loop-type\",\n      \"packetKind\": \"workflow\",\n      \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": false,\n      \"toolSurface\": {\n        \"allowed\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Edit\", \"Bash\", \"Grep\", \"Glob\", \"Task\"],\n        \"forbidden\": [],\n        \"mutatesWorkspace\": true,\n        \"bashAllowlist\": []\n      },\n      \"packet\": \"deep-review\",\n      \"command\": \"/deep:review\",\n      \"agent\": \"deep-review\",\n      \"artifactRoot\": \"review/\",\n      \"aliases\": [\"deep-review\", \"review loop\", \"iterative review loop\", \"severity weighted findings\", \"convergence review\", \"release-readiness\", \"deep-review wave\"],\n      \"advisorRouting\": {\n        \"routingClass\": \"lexical\",\n        \"legacyAdvisorId\": \"deep-review\",\n        \"legacyAliases\": [\"command-spec-kit-deep-review\", \"/deep:review\", \"spec_kit:deep-review\", \"deep-review\", \"sk-deep-review\"],\n        \"packetSkillName\": \"deep-review\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"workflowMode\": \"ai-council\",\n      \"runtimeLoopType\": \"council\",\n      \"backendKind\": \"runtime-loop-type\",\n      \"packetKind\": \"workflow\",\n      \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": false,\n      \"toolSurface\": {\n        \"allowed\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Edit\", \"Bash\", \"Grep\", \"Glob\", \"Task\"],\n        \"forbidden\": [],\n        \"mutatesWorkspace\": true,\n        \"bashAllowlist\": []\n      },\n      \"packet\": \"deep-ai-council\",\n      \"command\": \"/deep:ai-council\",\n      \"agent\": \"ai-council\",\n      \"artifactRoot\": \"ai-council/\",\n      \"aliases\": [\"deep-ai-council\", \"ai council deliberation\", \"multi-seat planning council\", \"council convergence\", \"planning council\"],\n      \"advisorRouting\": {\n        \"routingClass\": \"lexical\",\n        \"legacyAdvisorId\": \"deep-ai-council\",\n        \"legacyAliases\": [\"@deep-ai-council\", \"deep-ai-council\", \"deep ai council\", \"ai council\", \"planning council\", \"council deliberation\", \"multi-ai-council\"],\n        \"packetSkillName\": \"deep-ai-council\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"workflowMode\": \"agent-improvement\",\n      \"runtimeLoopType\": null,\n      \"backendKind\": \"improvement-host\",\n      \"packetKind\": \"workflow\",\n      \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": false,\n      \"toolSurface\": {\n        \"allowed\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Edit\", \"Bash\", \"Grep\", \"Glob\", \"Task\"],\n        \"forbidden\": [],\n        \"mutatesWorkspace\": true,\n        \"bashAllowlist\": []\n      },\n      \"packet\": \"deep-improvement\",\n      \"loopHostMode\": \"agent-improvement\",\n      \"command\": \"/deep:agent-improvement\",\n      \"agent\": \"deep-improvement\",\n      \"artifactRoot\": \"improvement/\",\n      \"aliases\": [\"improve agent\", \"evaluate agent\", \"agent scoring\", \"score agent candidate\", \"promote or rollback agent change\", \"agent-improvement\"],\n      \"advisorRouting\": {\n        \"routingClass\": \"alias-fold\",\n        \"legacyAdvisorId\": \"deep-improvement\",\n        \"advisorDefaultMode\": true,\n        \"legacyAliases\": [\"command-spec-kit-deep-agent-improvement\", \"/deep:agent-improvement\", \"deep-agent-improvement\", \"sk-deep-agent-improvement\"],\n        \"packetSkillName\": \"deep-improvement\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"workflowMode\": \"model-benchmark\",\n      \"runtimeLoopType\": null,\n      \"backendKind\": \"improvement-host\",\n      \"packetKind\": \"workflow\",\n      \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": false,\n      \"toolSurface\": {\n        \"allowed\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Edit\", \"Bash\", \"Grep\", \"Glob\", \"Task\"],\n        \"forbidden\": [],\n        \"mutatesWorkspace\": true,\n        \"bashAllowlist\": []\n      },\n      \"packet\": \"deep-improvement\",\n      \"loopHostMode\": \"model-benchmark\",\n      \"command\": \"/deep:model-benchmark\",\n      \"agent\": \"deep-improvement\",\n      \"artifactRoot\": \"improvement/\",\n      \"aliases\": [\"model benchmark\", \"benchmark a model\", \"prompt framework benchmark\", \"benchmark-harness\"],\n      \"advisorRouting\": {\n        \"routingClass\": \"command-bridge\",\n        \"packetSkillName\": \"deep-improvement\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"workflowMode\": \"skill-benchmark\",\n      \"runtimeLoopType\": null,\n      \"backendKind\": \"improvement-host\",\n      \"packetKind\": \"workflow\",\n      \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": false,\n      \"toolSurface\": {\n        \"allowed\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Edit\", \"Bash\", \"Grep\", \"Glob\", \"Task\"],\n        \"forbidden\": [],\n        \"mutatesWorkspace\": true,\n        \"bashAllowlist\": []\n      },\n      \"packet\": \"deep-improvement\",\n      \"loopHostMode\": \"skill-benchmark\",\n      \"command\": \"/deep:skill-benchmark\",\n      \"agent\": \"deep-improvement\",\n      \"artifactRoot\": \"improvement/\",\n      \"aliases\": [\"skill benchmark\", \"benchmark a skill\", \"skill routing benchmark\"],\n      \"advisorRouting\": {\n        \"routingClass\": \"command-bridge\",\n        \"packetSkillName\": \"deep-improvement\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"workflowMode\": \"alignment\",\n      \"runtimeLoopType\": \"review\",\n      \"backendKind\": \"runtime-loop-type\",\n      \"packetKind\": \"workflow\",\n      \"grandfatheredFolderMismatch\": false,\n      \"toolSurface\": {\n        \"allowed\": [\"Read\", \"Grep\", \"Glob\", \"Task\", \"Bash\"],\n        \"forbidden\": [\"Write\", \"Edit\"],\n        \"mutatesWorkspace\": true,\n        \"bashAllowlist\": []\n      },\n      \"packet\": \"deep-alignment\",\n      \"command\": \"/deep:alignment\",\n      \"agent\": \"deep-alignment\",\n      \"artifactRoot\": \"alignment/\",\n      \"aliases\": [\"deep-alignment\", \"/deep:command-benchmark\", \"alignment lane\", \"conformance review\", \"standard authority check\", \"alignment conformance audit\"],\n      \"advisorRouting\": {\n        \"routingClass\": \"lexical\",\n        \"legacyAdvisorId\": \"deep-alignment\",\n        \"legacyAliases\": [\"command-spec-kit-deep-alignment\", \"/deep:alignment\", \"spec_kit:deep-alignment\", \"deep-alignment\", \"sk-deep-alignment\"],\n        \"packetSkillName\": \"deep-alignment\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n---\nname: deep-research\ndescription: \"Autonomous deep-research loop: iterative investigation, externalized state, convergence detection, fresh context per pass.\"\nallowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task, WebFetch, memory_context, memory_search]\nargument-hint: \"[topic] [:auto|:confirm] [--max-iterations=N] [--convergence=N]\"\nversion: 1.14.0.0\n---\n\n<!-- Keywords: autoresearch, deep-research, iterative-research, autonomous-loop, convergence-detection, externalized-state, fresh-context, research-agent, JSONL-state, strategy-file -->\n\n# Autonomous Deep Research Loop\n\nNote: `Task` is allowed for the command executor that manages the loop. The `@deep-research` agent itself is LEAF-only and does not dispatch sub-agents.\n\nIterative research protocol with fresh context per iteration, externalized state, and convergence detection for deep technical investigation.\n\nRuntime path resolution: OpenCode/Copilot runtime uses `.opencode/agents/*.md`; Claude runtime uses `.claude/agents/*.md`.\n\nOperator contract precedence for this skill surface (highest first): command entrypoint syntax in `.opencode/commands/deep/research.md`; convergence math in `references/convergence/convergence.md` and the deep-research YAML workflow; runtime agent inventories from the checked-in runtime directories above.\n\n### Convergence Threshold Semantics\n\n**Default:** 0.05 on newInfoRatio (fully-new=1.0, partially-new=0.5, +0.10 simplicity bonus, capped 1.0)\n\n**Semantic:** `convergenceThreshold` compares newly discovered information against accumulated research knowledge with negative-knowledge emphasis. Lower = more iterations / higher signal threshold.\n\n**NOT INTERCHANGEABLE with siblings:**\n- `deep-review` uses 0.10 default on weighted P0/P1/P2 severity ratio\n- `deep-ai-council` uses 0.20 default on adjudicator-verdict stability\n\nCarrying threshold expectations across siblings will cause unexpected iteration counts; see this skill's changelog/decision records for the parity research confirming thresholds do not carry across siblings.\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\n### Activation Triggers\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Deep investigation requiring multiple rounds of discovery\n- Topic spans 3+ technical domains or sources\n- Initial findings need progressive refinement\n- Overnight or unattended research sessions\n- Research where prior findings inform subsequent queries\n\nKeyword triggers:\n\n- `autoresearch`\n- `deep research`\n- `autonomous research`\n- `research loop`\n- `iterative research`\n- `multi-round research`\n- `deep investigation`\n- `comprehensive research`\n\n### Use Cases\n\nUse deep-research for multi-round technical investigation, source triangulation, repeated exploration with fresh context, and research sessions where prior findings should shape the next focus.\n\n### When NOT to Use\n\n- Simple, single-question research (use direct codebase search or `/speckit:plan`)\n- Known-solution documentation (use `/speckit:plan`)\n- Implementation tasks (use `/speckit:implement`)\n- Quick codebase searches (use `@context` or direct Grep/Glob)\n- Fewer than 3 sources needed (single-pass research suffices)\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\n> Pattern: aligned with the [sk-doc smart-router resilience template](../../sk-doc/create-skill/assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md).\n\n### Resource Domains\n\nThe router discovers markdown resources from `references/` and `assets/`, then applies intent scoring from `RESOURCE_MAP`. Keep routing domain-focused rather than hardcoding exhaustive inventories.\n\n- `references/guides/quick-reference.md` -- first-touch operator cheat sheet.\n- `references/protocol/loop-protocol.md` -- lifecycle, dispatch, reducer sequencing, command-owned state flow.\n- `references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md` -- bounded `spec.md` anchoring and generated-fence write-back.\n- `references/convergence*.md` -- stop contracts, signals, recovery, graph gates, reference-only convergence ideas.\n- `references/state*.md` -- packet layout, JSONL records, markdown outputs, reducer ownership, reconstruction.\n- `references/guides/capability-matrix.md` -- runtime parity.\n- `assets/*.md` -- markdown templates and prompt assets safe for guarded markdown loading.\n\n### Resource Loading Levels\n\n| Level | When to Load | Resources |\n|-------|--------------|-----------|\n| ALWAYS | Every skill invocation | Quick reference baseline |\n| CONDITIONAL | If intent signals match | Loop, convergence, state, spec anchoring, runtime parity references |\n| ON_DEMAND | Only on explicit request | Full reference set and markdown assets |\n\n### Phase Signals\n\n| Phase | Signal | Primary Resources |\n|-------|--------|-------------------|\n| Init | No JSONL exists or setup context | `loop-protocol.md`, `state-format.md`, `state-jsonl.md` |\n| Iteration | Dispatch context includes iteration number | `loop-protocol.md`, `state-outputs.md`, `convergence-signals.md` |\n| Stuck | Dispatch context includes recovery language | `convergence-recovery.md`, `state-reducer-registry.md` |\n| Synthesis | STOP candidate or final report | `convergence.md`, `state-outputs.md`, `spec-check-protocol.md` |\n\n### Smart Router Pseudocode\n\nThe authoritative routing logic for scoped loading, weighted intent scoring, ambiguity handling, and graceful fallback, via four patterns: runtime discovery (`discover_markdown_resources()` scans `references/`/`assets/`), existence-check-before-load (`load_if_available()` guards paths against `inventory` and `seen`), extensible routing keys (intent labels map to resource families, not static file lists), and multi-tier graceful fallback (`UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST` for disambiguation; missing families return a helpful notice).\n\n```python\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSKILL_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nRESOURCE_BASES = (SKILL_ROOT / \"references\", SKILL_ROOT / \"assets\")\nDEFAULT_RESOURCE = \"references/guides/quick-reference.md\"\n\nINTENT_SIGNALS = {\n    \"LOOP_SETUP\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"autoresearch\", \"deep research\", \"research loop\", \"autonomous research\", \"setup\", \"init\"]},\n    \"ITERATION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"iteration\", \"next round\", \"continue research\", \"research cycle\", \"delta\", \"focus\"]},\n    \"CONVERGENCE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"convergence\", \"stop condition\", \"diminishing returns\", \"legal stop\", \"newInfoRatio\"]},\n    \"RECOVERY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"stuck\", \"recovery\", \"timeout\", \"reconstruct\", \"blocked stop\", \"blocked_stop\"]},\n    \"STATE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"state file\", \"jsonl\", \"strategy\", \"dashboard\", \"registry\", \"lineage\"]},\n    \"SPEC_ANCHORING\": {\"weight\": 3, \"keywords\": [\"spec.md\", \"generated fence\", \"folder_state\", \"lock\", \"spec anchoring\"]},\n    \"RUNTIME_PARITY\": {\"weight\": 3, \"keywords\": [\"runtime\", \"capability\", \"parity\", \"opencode\", \"claude\"]},\n    \"RESOURCE_MAP\": {\"weight\": 3, \"keywords\": [\"resource map\", \"resource-map\", \"inventory\", \"coverage gate\"]},\n}\n\nRESOURCE_MAP = {\n    \"LOOP_SETUP\": [\"references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\", \"references/state/state-format.md\", \"references/state/state-jsonl.md\", \"references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md\", \"references/protocol/context-snapshot.md\"],\n    \"ITERATION\": [\"references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\", \"references/state/state-outputs.md\", \"references/convergence/convergence-signals.md\"],\n    \"CONVERGENCE\": [\"references/convergence/convergence.md\", \"references/convergence/convergence-signals.md\", \"references/convergence/convergence-graph.md\"],\n    \"RECOVERY\": [\"references/convergence/convergence-recovery.md\", \"references/state/state-reducer-registry.md\"],\n    \"STATE\": [\"references/state/state-format.md\", \"references/state/state-jsonl.md\", \"references/state/state-outputs.md\", \"references/state/state-reducer-registry.md\", \"assets/deep-research-strategy.md\"],\n    \"SPEC_ANCHORING\": [\"references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md\", \"references/state/state-outputs.md\"],\n    \"RUNTIME_PARITY\": [\"references/guides/capability-matrix.md\"],\n    \"RESOURCE_MAP\": [\"references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\", \"references/state/state-outputs.md\"],\n}\n\nLOADING_LEVELS = {\n    \"ALWAYS\": [DEFAULT_RESOURCE],\n    \"ON_DEMAND_KEYWORDS\": [\"full protocol\", \"all references\", \"complete reference\", \"resume deep research\", \"state log\", \"research/iterations\", \"deltas\", \"overnight research\", \"active lineage\", \"reference-only\", \"optimizer\"],\n    \"ON_DEMAND\": [\n        \"references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\",\n        \"references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md\",\n        \"references/convergence/convergence.md\",\n        \"references/convergence/convergence-signals.md\",\n        \"references/convergence/convergence-recovery.md\",\n        \"references/convergence/convergence-graph.md\",\n        \"references/convergence/convergence-reference-only.md\",\n        \"references/state/state-format.md\",\n        \"references/state/state-jsonl.md\",\n        \"references/state/state-outputs.md\",\n        \"references/state/state-reducer-registry.md\",\n        \"references/guides/capability-matrix.md\",\n    ],\n}\n\nUNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n    \"Confirm setup vs iteration vs convergence vs state recovery\",\n    \"Confirm the target spec folder and research packet\",\n    \"Provide the current phase, latest iteration, or failing state file\",\n    \"Confirm whether full references or quick routing guidance are needed\",\n]\n\ndef _task_text(task) -> str:\n    return \" \".join([\n        str(getattr(task, \"text\", \"\")),\n        str(getattr(task, \"query\", \"\")),\n        \" \".join(getattr(task, \"keywords\", []) or []),\n    ]).lower()\n\ndef _guard_in_skill(relative_path: str) -> str:\n    resolved = (SKILL_ROOT / relative_path).resolve()\n    resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT)\n    if resolved.suffix.lower() != \".md\":\n        raise ValueError(f\"Only markdown resources are routable: {relative_path}\")\n    return resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix()\n\ndef _guard_resource_map(resource_map: dict[str, list[str]]) -> None:\n    for intent, resources in resource_map.items():\n        for relative_path in resources:\n            guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n            if guarded.startswith(\"references/\"):\n                tail = guarded.removeprefix(\"references/\")\n                if \"/\" not in tail and \"-\" in Path(tail).stem:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"RESOURCE_MAP must target canonical references, not compatibility stubs: {intent} -> {guarded}\")\n\ndef discover_markdown_resources() -> set[str]:\n    docs = []\n    for base in RESOURCE_BASES:\n        if base.exists():\n            docs.extend(path for path in base.rglob(\"*.md\") if path.is_file())\n    return {doc.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix() for doc in docs}\n\ndef score_intents(task) -> dict[str, float]:\n    text = _task_text(task)\n    scores = {intent: 0.0 for intent in INTENT_SIGNALS}\n    for intent, cfg in INTENT_SIGNALS.items():\n        for keyword in cfg[\"keywords\"]:\n            if keyword in text:\n                scores[intent] += cfg[\"weight\"]\n    return scores\n\ndef select_intents(scores: dict[str, float], ambiguity_delta: float = 1.0, max_intents: int = 2) -> list[str]:\n    ranked = sorted(scores.items(), key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n    if not ranked or ranked[0][1] <= 0:\n        return [\"LOOP_SETUP\"]\n    selected = [ranked[0][0]]\n    if len(ranked) > 1 and ranked[1][1] > 0 and (ranked[0][1] - ranked[1][1]) <= ambiguity_delta:\n        selected.append(ranked[1][0])\n    return selected[:max_intents]\n\ndef route_deep_research_resources(task):\n    _guard_resource_map(RESOURCE_MAP)\n    _guard_resource_map({\"ALWAYS\": LOADING_LEVELS[\"ALWAYS\"], \"ON_DEMAND\": LOADING_LEVELS[\"ON_DEMAND\"]})\n    inventory = discover_markdown_resources()\n    scores = score_intents(task)\n    intents = select_intents(scores)\n    loaded = []\n    seen = set()\n\n    def load_if_available(relative_path: str) -> None:\n        guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n        if guarded in inventory and guarded not in seen:\n            load(guarded)\n            loaded.append(guarded)\n            seen.add(guarded)\n\n    for relative_path in LOADING_LEVELS[\"ALWAYS\"]:\n        load_if_available(relative_path)\n\n    if max(scores.values() or [0]) < 0.5:\n        return {\n            \"intents\": intents,\n            \"intent_scores\": scores,\n            \"load_level\": \"UNKNOWN_FALLBACK\",\n            \"needs_disambiguation\": True,\n            \"disambiguation_checklist\": UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST,\n            \"resources\": loaded,\n        }\n\n    matched_intents = []\n    for intent in intents:\n        before_count = len(loaded)\n        for relative_path in RESOURCE_MAP.get(intent, []):\n            load_if_available(relative_path)\n        if len(loaded) > before_count:\n            matched_intents.append(intent)\n\n    text = _task_text(task)\n    if any(keyword in text for keyword in LOADING_LEVELS[\"ON_DEMAND_KEYWORDS\"]):\n        for relative_path in LOADING_LEVELS[\"ON_DEMAND\"]:\n            load_if_available(relative_path)\n\n    result = {\"intents\": intents, \"intent_scores\": scores, \"resources\": loaded}\n    if not matched_intents:\n        result[\"notice\"] = f\"No knowledge base found for intent(s): {', '.join(intents)}\"\n    return result\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Invocation Contract\n\nThis skill is invoked exclusively through `/deep:research:auto` or `/deep:research:confirm` -- the command YAML owns state, dispatch, convergence, and synthesis. Never simulate the loop with ad hoc shell dispatch, nested CLI loops, direct `@deep-research` Task dispatch, `/tmp` prompt files, or state outside the resolved local research packet.\n\n### Executor Selection Contract\n\nThe YAML workflow owns executor selection (native `@deep-research` by default, or a routed CLI executor -- never ad hoc shell loops). Cross-CLI delegation inside an executor sandbox is possible but discouraged: do not invoke the same CLI from within itself, and do not assume auth propagates to child CLIs. Per-kind dispatch branches (`native`, `cli-opencode`, `cli-claude-code`) and flag-compatibility rules are in [loop-protocol.md §3](references/protocol/loop-protocol.md).\n\nExecutor invariants:\n\n1. Produce a non-empty iteration markdown file at `{state_paths.iteration_pattern}`.\n2. Append a JSONL delta record to `{state_paths.state_log}` with required fields: `type`, `iteration`, `newInfoRatio`, `status`, and `focus`.\n3. Respect the LEAF-agent constraint: no sub-dispatch, no nested loops, and max 12 tool calls per iteration.\n\nFailure modes include `iteration_file_missing`, `iteration_file_empty`, `jsonl_not_appended`, `jsonl_missing_fields`, and `jsonl_parse_error`. Three consecutive failures route to stuck recovery.\n\n### Lifecycle Contract\n\nRuntime-supported lifecycle modes:\n\n| Mode | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `new` | First run against the spec folder |\n| `resume` | Continue the active lineage and append a typed `resumed` JSONL event |\n| `restart` | Archive the existing research tree, mint a fresh `sessionId`, increment `generation`, and append a typed `restarted` event |\n\nDeferred modes `fork` and `completed-continue` are reserved but not runtime-supported.\n\n### Code-Graph Readiness TrustState Surface\n\nThe live code-graph readiness contract reaches four TrustState values: `live`, `stale`, `absent`, and `unavailable`. `cached`, `imported`, `rebuilt`, and `rehomed` remain declared in the shared TrustState type for compatibility, but the readiness helpers used here do not emit them today.\n\n### Resource Map Integration\n\nWhen `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` exists at init, `resource_map_present: true` is persisted, the map is summarized into `deep-research-strategy.md` `Known Context`, and listed files count as known inventory (gaps flagged only when missing from the map). When absent, `resource_map_present: false` is persisted and the loop continues normally -- absence is informational, not a failure. Full field-level rules live in [state-outputs.md §6](references/state/state-outputs.md).\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot Replacement\n\nFor codebase-scoped targets, initialization captures a bounded, pointer-based snapshot (source paths/symbols, integration points, conventions, and gaps) into `deep-research-strategy.md` `Known Context` -- oriented toward the first iteration, not a substitute for `@context` or `/speckit:plan`. Full capture rules and routing guidance live in [context-snapshot.md](references/protocol/context-snapshot.md).\n\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n -i \"surface|sub[- ]language|sublanguage|webflow|opencode\" .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop' in /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover\n succeeded in 0ms:\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:20:Use this skill (through the hub) for any active deep-loop workflow. Invoke it as `Skill(system-deep-loop)` (optionally with a mode hint such as `research: <request>` or `alignment: <request>`); the hub classifies the request, resolves a `workflowMode`, and loads the matching nested mode packet. Active `/deep:*` commands and native agent types remain as complementary surfaces over the same packets.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:38:Routing is **registry-driven** (invokable-hub, Option E). `mode-registry.json` is the single source of truth; the hub reads it and does not re-derive the mapping. When invoked as `Skill(system-deep-loop[, \"<mode>: <request>\"])`, the hub classifies the request to a `workflowMode`, resolves it through the registry, and loads `registry[mode].packet`. The advisor routes any deep-loop query to the single identity `system-deep-loop`; the hub then picks the mode. The `/deep:*` commands and native agent types remain as complementary surfaces — they reach the same packets through static routers/agent definitions — and the hub holds NO per-mode logic.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:42:> node .opencode/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub system-deep-loop --prompt \"<task>\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:46:This hub is an intent/registry router, not a keyed resource-discovery router: at runtime it omits `discover_markdown_resources` and only guards registry-selected packet loads, never selecting hub-level `references/<key>/` or `assets/<key>/` resources by runtime key. It does carry a second-layer surface router at `shared/references/smart-routing.md` — a benchmark/replay artifact (mirroring sk-prompt/sk-code) that maps a resolved mode's intent to packet-qualified child leaves so router-replay can emit canonical `{workflowMode, leafResourceId}` typed pairs against `leaf-manifest.json`. That surface layer never re-decides the mode and is not a runtime hub discovery surface; the hub still routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json` alone.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:50:The hub's own routing logic is read-only (classify, guard a path, load a packet). The frontmatter `allowed-tools` list is nonetheless broad because, per the two-axis hub canon contract, a hub's tool grant MUST equal the exact union of every registered mode's `toolSurface.allowed` in `mode-registry.json` — not the tool set the hub's own logic uses. This is a hard invariant enforced by `parent-skill-check.cjs` (check 3j: \"hub allowed-tools equals the union of mode tool surfaces\"); narrowing the frontmatter grant to only what routing-only logic needs would fail that check and break every mode whose `toolSurface` isn't a subset of the narrowed list. Treat the breadth of `allowed-tools` as evidence of the child modes' combined needs, not of mutating logic living in the hub.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:78:Per-mode behavior is **not flattened**: each active packet keeps its own convergence math, state shape, artifacts, and tool-permission guards (research has WebFetch; review/ai-council are code/inward-only; alignment is a named-standard, read-only-by-default conformance audit; improvement is the only direct mutation family). Exactly one `graph-metadata.json` — this hub's — is preserved, so the advisor discovers exactly one skill identity regardless of which surface (hub `Skill()`, `/deep:*` command, or agent) reaches a mode.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:94:Each active mode packet keeps its own `SKILL.md`, `references/`, `scripts/`, `assets/`, `feature-catalog/`, or `manual-testing-playbook/` as applicable, with internal paths repointed and **no per-packet `graph-metadata.json`** — only this hub carries one, so the advisor discovers exactly one skill. The `deep-ai-council` packet folder follows the standard `folder == packetSkillName` convention (`deep-ai-council`); its legacy public surfaces (the `/deep:ai-council` command and the `ai-council` agent) intentionally keep the shorter `ai-council` key, so always resolve the packet path through `mode-registry.json` rather than hardcoding it.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:108:- **ALWAYS** keep `Skill(system-deep-loop)` hub routing, the `/deep:*` commands, and the agent types as complementary surfaces over the same packets — never let one surface fork per-mode logic out of its packet.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:124:- Backend: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/` (frozen, consumed by every mode; nested infrastructure, not a separate skill).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:126:- Commands: the active `/deep:*` commands under `.opencode/commands/deep/` (complementary surface).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:149:### Surfaces and Consumers\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:150:- `Skill(system-deep-loop)` is the invokable hub; active `/deep:*` commands and the agent types (`deep-research`, `deep-review`, `ai-council`, `deep-improvement`, `deep-alignment`) are complementary surfaces over the same packets.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:158:- Pattern: `.opencode/skills/sk-doc/create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md` (parent-skill hub + nested packets, the one-graph-metadata invariant).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:159:- Sibling example: `.opencode/skills/sk-design/` (the same invokable-hub + `mode-registry.json` Option E pattern).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/assets/runtime-capabilities.json:13:    \"opencode\": {\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/assets/runtime-capabilities.json:14:      \"agentPath\": \".opencode/agents/ai-council.md\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/assets/runtime-capabilities.json:17:      \"notes\": \"OpenCode supplies in-runtime model diversity when available.\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/assets/runtime-capabilities.json:27:    \"quickValidate\": \"python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/quick_validate.py .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council --json\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/assets/runtime-capabilities.json:28:    \"completionAdvisory\": \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/advise-council-completion.cjs <packet>\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/baselines/claude-baseline.md:40:  `opencode`. Host bootstrap folds into every latency ratio.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-005-orchestrate-handoff.md:8:  \"entry_surface\": \"E4\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-005-orchestrate-handoff.md:10:  \"prompt\": \"Use your council process to decide the rate-limit strategy for .opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-003-council-target — convene diverse seats and converge, do not just pick one yourself.\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-005-orchestrate-handoff.md:12:  \"fixture\": \".opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-003-council-target\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/README.md:112:Adding another active mode (a new packet beyond `deep-research`, `deep-review`, `deep-ai-council`, `deep-improvement`, `deep-alignment`) touches every one of these surfaces — miss one and the mode is either unroutable, undiscoverable, or drift-guard-broken:\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/README.md:114:- [ ] **`mode-registry.json`** — add the mode's registry entry: `workflowMode`, `runtimeLoopType` (or explicit `null`), `backendKind`, `packet`, `packetKind`, `toolSurface`, `advisorRouting`, and `aliases`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/README.md:116:- [ ] **`SKILL.md`** — add a row to the §1 WHEN TO USE mode table (mode, use-it-for, packet, command, agent), and update the frontmatter `allowed-tools` if the new mode's `toolSurface.allowed` introduces a tool no existing mode grants (keep it equal to the union — see §2 SMART ROUTING).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/README.md:119:- [ ] **`node .opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop`** — re-run after all of the above; it validates registry shape, alias uniqueness, tool-surface union (3j), and hub-router consistency in one pass.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-004-concise-natural-ask.md:8:  \"entry_surface\": \"E3\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-004-concise-natural-ask.md:10:  \"prompt\": \"convene a council on the rate-limit design question in .opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-003-council-target/spec.md and recommend an approach\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-004-concise-natural-ask.md:12:  \"fixture\": \".opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-003-council-target\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-003-vague-natural-ask.md:8:  \"entry_surface\": \"E3\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-003-vague-natural-ask.md:12:  \"fixture\": \".opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-003-council-target\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v2.4.0.0.md:11:> Spec folder: `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/155-parent-skill-native-invocability/002-deep-loop-alignment` (Level 3)\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:1:First major iteration of `deep-ai-council` after the initial v1.0.0.0 skill release. This series ships a dedicated council graph as a derived projection (Phase 003), full operator playbook coverage of that graph (Phase 004), 6 fix-ups and value-comparison scenarios proving the graph beats the no-graph baseline (Phase 005), CI-protected fixture-driven value vitest with measured ratios (Phase 006), runnable test-gate infrastructure plus 32-entry feature catalog plus reverse-anchor meta-test plus replay helper plus Codex TOML parity plus fixture provenance (Phase 007), and skill-surface polish plus this changelog plus smoke coverage for the new helper scripts (Phase 008). All seven phases land in 101 as additive child packets; runtime code and authoritative artifact contracts stay unchanged.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:3:> Spec folders: `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/101-deep-multi-ai-council-skill/{003-deep-ai-council-graph-support, 004-deep-ai-council-playbook-graph-coverage, 005-deep-ai-council-fixups-and-graph-value-scenarios, 006-council-graph-value-scenario-automation, 007-council-infrastructure-hardening, 008-council-surface-polish}` (Level 1-3 across the six phases)\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:11:A derived SQLite projection now indexes council deliberation as graph rows. Four MCP tools own the surface — `council_graph_upsert`, `council_graph_query`, `council_graph_status`, `council_graph_convergence` — registered as a distinct family from the existing `deep_loop_graph_*` research/review graph. Eight node kinds (SESSION, ROUND, SEAT, CLAIM, EVIDENCE, DISAGREEMENT, DECISION, RECOMMENDATION), ten relation kinds (PARTICIPATES_IN, PROPOSES, SUPPORTS, CONTRADICTS, DERIVES_FROM, AGREES_WITH, RESOLVES, ESCALATES, EVIDENCE_FOR, RECOMMENDS), five query modes (`unresolved_disagreements`, `evidence_chain`, `decision_support`, `convergence_blockers`, `hot_nodes`), and three convergence buckets (`STOP_ALLOWED`, `CONTINUE`, `STOP_BLOCKED`) cover the full council deliberation lifecycle. ADR-001 documents the dedicated-projection decision over deep-loop graph reuse. Artifacts under `ai-council/**` stay authoritative — the graph rebuilds from them.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:17:The manual testing playbook grew from 18 to 32 scenarios across 9 categories. Phase 004 added 8 functional graph integration scenarios (DAC-019..DAC-026) one-to-one with the shipped MCP surface — idempotent upsert + self-loop rejection, empty-input no-op, hostile-metadata redaction, five query modes, three convergence buckets, recovery payload, derived-projection replay contract, tool-family separation. Phase 005 added 6 value-comparison scenarios (DAC-027..DAC-032) that contrast the no-graph operator baseline workflow against the with-graph workflow on real-world situations: unresolved-disagreement triage, decision provenance audit, convergence safety under critical disagreement (the graph blocks a stop the naive two-of-three baseline would allow), stalled-council blocker ranking, hot-topic discovery, mid-run interruption recovery. Phase 005 also repaired two pre-existing vitest failures (Claude translated frontmatter parity assertion, stale persist-artifacts HELPER_PATH).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:29:The council vitest matrix is now one command: `npm run --prefix .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server test:council` runs nine vitest files in ~2 seconds. The standalone bash runner at `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/test-council-matrix.sh` wraps that matrix with sk-doc validation plus strict parent spec validation. A 32-entry feature catalog under `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/feature-catalog/` mirrors the playbook 1:1, replacing the previous \"No feature catalog exists yet\" placeholders. A reverse-anchor meta-test at `mcp-server/tests/council-playbook-anchor-integrity.vitest.ts` reads the playbook and asserts every referenced vitest file and test-name string resolves to a real test — so renaming a test name surfaces a playbook update need immediately. The DAC-025 replay path is now executable via `scripts/replay-graph-from-artifacts.cjs` — a pure-Node CJS helper that reads `ai-council-state.jsonl` and emits a `council_graph_upsert` payload. The Codex TOML runtime mirror's name and description prose now have parity assertions alongside the existing sandbox/permissions checks. Inline normalization comments in `tests/fixtures/council-value/seed-helpers.ts` document why DAC-030 and DAC-032 fixture-side answers are derived from grouped runtime responses.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:33:### Skill-Surface Polish (Phase 008)\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:35:This final phase surfaces the new artifacts through the skill entry point. SKILL.md now references `feature-catalog/` and `scripts/replay-graph-from-artifacts.cjs` in the Resource Domains section. The smoke vitest at `tests/council-helpers-smoke.vitest.ts` covers the replay helper end-to-end on a synthetic JSONL fixture plus a shape assertion on the bash runner. The `test:council` npm script grew to ten vitest files.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:73:- `node .opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/scripts/replay-graph-from-artifacts.cjs --spec-folder <path> --session-id <id> [--dry-run]` — read `ai-council-state.jsonl` and emit a `council_graph_upsert` payload for operator-piped MCP replay.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:74:- `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/test-council-matrix.sh` — run the full council vitest matrix plus sk-doc + strict spec validation in one command.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/replay-graph-from-artifacts.cjs:22:  node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/replay-graph-from-artifacts.cjs --spec-folder <path> --session-id <id> [--dry-run]\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/replay-graph-from-artifacts.cjs:26:  node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --loop-type council\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/replay-graph-from-artifacts.cjs:55:      fs.existsSync(path.join(current, '.opencode'))\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/replay-graph-from-artifacts.cjs:56:      && fs.existsSync(path.join(current, '.opencode', 'skills', 'system-deep-loop', 'runtime', 'scripts', 'upsert.cjs'))\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/replay-graph-from-artifacts.cjs:65:    || path.join(repoRoot, '.opencode', 'skills', 'system-deep-loop', 'runtime', 'scripts', 'upsert.cjs');\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark.md:5:  measure executor-model behavior at the /deep:ai-council command surface under\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/behavior-benchmark.md:19:`/deep:ai-council` command surface is triggered with a realistic user prompt.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md:21:This document is the single source of truth for the `@deep-ai-council` §8 OUTPUT FORMAT. The agent body uses §8 to tell the planning LEAF what report to return; `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs` uses this contract to parse that report and persist packet-local `ai-council/` artifacts.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md:27:- Agent body: `.opencode/agents/ai-council.md` §8 OUTPUT FORMAT and §16 Caller Persistence Protocol\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md:29:- Helper: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md:79:### Seat 001 - Analytical / cli-opencode\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md:88:- `### Seat 001 - Analytical / cli-opencode`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md:89:- `### Seat 1: Analytical / cli-opencode`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md:90:- `#### Seat-001 Analytical / cli-opencode`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md:99:| seat-001 | Analytical | cli-opencode | Check implementation sequence | 84 |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md:131:3. Update `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md:135:Do not change one surface alone. Split-brain between §8 prose, parser behavior, and fixtures makes persisted council artifacts unreliable.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md:20:The council is **primarily an IN-CLI capability**. When invoked from inside an active runtime (OpenCode, Claude Code, OpenCode), the council deliberates using THAT runtime's own models and reasoning lenses as seats. No external dispatch is required for the common case — the active CLI's own model bench (e.g. Opus + Sonnet + Haiku on Claude Code; gpt-5.5 + gpt-5.5-pro + gpt-5.5-xhigh on OpenCode; direct DeepSeek, Xiaomi, and OpenAI provider models on OpenCode) supplies the seat diversity for a round.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md:22:**External-CLI dispatch is a SECONDARY, optional mode** for cases where a different AI vantage adds value (e.g. a fresh OpenCode perspective from inside a Claude Code session, or DeepSeek/Kimi via cli-opencode from inside another runtime). It is invoked via the `cli-*` skill family (`cli-claude-code`, `cli-opencode`) — never directly from this skill.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md:26:- External-CLI round: all seats use ONE external CLI (e.g. all `cli-claude-code` seats with different reasoning levels, OR all `cli-opencode` seats with different direct-provider models).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md:327:node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs <packet> --input-file <report>\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md:328:node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/advise-council-completion.cjs <packet>\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md:342:   - This preserves the planning-only boundary and avoids mutating implementation or spec-doc surfaces.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md:357:   - All seats within ONE deliberation round MUST be dispatched through the SAME CLI executor (e.g. all seats from `cli-claude-code`, OR all seats from `cli-opencode`, OR all seats from `cli-opencode`). Seat diversity WITHIN a round comes from different models/reasoning lenses on the same CLI (e.g. `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro --variant high` + `xiaomi/mimo-v2.5-pro`).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md:358:   - Mixing executors within one round (e.g. one seat via OpenCode + one seat via OpenCode + one seat via Claude Code) is FORBIDDEN — it conflates orchestration boundaries, complicates rollback, and produces noisy convergence signals because per-CLI guarantees (sandbox, runtime, tool surface, output schema) differ.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md:410:- `references/integration/graph-support.md` - derived council graph boundaries, tool surface, and recovery behavior.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md:431:- ✅ Council requests route to the `deep-ai-council` advisor/packet surface (`packetSkillName` and `legacyAdvisorId` in `mode-registry.json`); `deep-ai-council` is the packet folder/SKILL.md name (folder == name), while the dispatched agent identity remains `ai-council`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md:432:- ✅ Runtime mirrors dispatch `@ai-council` (`mode: subagent`, Task-dispatch only) under a consistent agent identity — both agent files (`.opencode/agents/ai-council.md`, `.claude/agents/ai-council.md`) declare `name: ai-council`, matching the registry `agent: ai-council` field.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md:457:Run `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh <spec-folder> --strict` before completion claims when spec docs are updated. Skill package structure is checked with `python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/quick_validate.py .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/leaf-manifest.json:209:        \"assets/conformance-benchmark/command-surface/conformance-benchmark.md\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/leaf-manifest.json:210:        \"assets/conformance-benchmark/command-surface/fixtures/fixture-manifest.json\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/leaf-manifest.json:211:        \"assets/conformance-benchmark/command-surface/lane-config.json\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/folder-layout.md:32:|   |-- round-001/                        # ONE CLI per round (e.g. all cli-opencode seats)\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/folder-layout.md:33:|   |   |-- seat-001-cli-opencode-gpt-5-5-high.md\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/folder-layout.md:34:|   |   |-- seat-002-cli-opencode-gpt-5-5-pro.md\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/folder-layout.md:35:|   |   |-- seat-003-cli-opencode-gpt-5-5-xhigh.md\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/folder-layout.md:64:**Canonical writer:** the council writes these artifacts directly with `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/persist-artifacts.cjs` named exports. Each writer is scoped to `ai-council/**` and appends an `artifact_written` audit event. `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs` remains a helper fallback for non-council callers.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/folder-layout.md:69:- Agent body: `.opencode/agents/ai-council.md` §12 OUTPUT PROTOCOL (this layout) + §13 INVOCATION CONTRACT + §14 STATE SCHEMA + §16 COUNCIL PERSISTENCE PROTOCOL + §18 ROLLBACK FOR OPERATORS\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/folder-layout.md:70:- Council writer library: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/persist-artifacts.cjs`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/folder-layout.md:71:- Helper fallback: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/folder-layout.md:72:- Schema: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/output-schema.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/folder-layout.md:73:- State format: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/state-format.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/folder-layout.md:74:- Command wiring: `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/patterns/command-wiring.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:27:This playbook provides 33 deterministic scenarios across 9 categories validating the `deep-ai-council` skill surface. Each feature keeps a `DAC-NNN` ID and links to a dedicated feature file with the full execution contract.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:29:Coverage note (2026-05-11): covers runtime rename, advisor routing, council deliberation, artifact persistence, state format, schema strictness, convergence, rollback, cross-mode anti-convergence floor, derived graph boundaries, planning-only boundaries, depth dispatch, failure handling, writer library sequence, scoring rubric use, adversarial critique, scoped-write rejection, the dedicated council-graph runtime CLI surface (upsert idempotency + self-loop rejection, empty-input no-op, hostile metadata redaction, five-mode prompt-safe queries, three-state convergence decision, recovery payload + readiness blocking, derived-projection replay, and retired MCP registry entries), and real-world value-comparison scenarios proving the graph beats the no-graph baseline for unresolved-disagreement triage, decision provenance audit, convergence safety under critical disagreement, stalled-council blocker ranking, hot-topic discovery, and mid-run interruption recovery.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:73:- CLI commands shown as `node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs <packet> --input-file <report>`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:82:bash: node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs <packet> --input-file <report>\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:83:bash: node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs <packet> --input-file <missing-required-section.md>; echo \"exit=$?\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:349:### DAC-026 | Council graph MCP surface retired\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:403:| `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/ai-council-runtime-parity.vitest.ts` | DAC-001 |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:404:| `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/scorer/native-scorer.vitest.ts` | DAC-002 |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:405:| `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/ai-council-permission-scope.vitest.ts` | DAC-003, DAC-004, DAC-011, DAC-012, DAC-017 |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:406:| `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/ai-council-audit-trail.vitest.ts` | DAC-005, DAC-006, DAC-013 |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:407:| `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/ai-council-rollback.vitest.ts` | DAC-010 |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:408:| `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/tests/ai-council-persist-artifacts.vitest.ts` | DAC-005, DAC-007 |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:409:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/council-graph-script.vitest.ts` | DAC-019, DAC-020, DAC-021, DAC-022, DAC-023, DAC-024 |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:410:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/council-graph-value-scenarios.vitest.ts` | DAC-027, DAC-028, DAC-029, DAC-030, DAC-031, DAC-032 |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:446:| DAC-026 | Council graph MCP surface retired | `council-graph-integration/council-graph-tools-registered-separately-from-deep-loop.md` | `feature-catalog/council-graph-integration/council-graph-tools-registered-separately-from-deep-loop.md` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/state-format.md:162:{\"schema_version\":\"1.2\",\"protocol\":\"ai-council\",\"producer\":\"persist-artifacts@1.2.0\",\"event\":\"artifact_written\",\"path\":\"seats/round-001/seat-001-cli-opencode.md\",\"bytes\":2048,\"checksum\":\"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-08T22:30:01.000Z\",\"seat_id\":\"seat-001\",\"round_id\":\"round-001\"}\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/state-format.md:163:{\"schema_version\":\"1.2\",\"protocol\":\"ai-council\",\"producer\":\"persist-artifacts@1.2.0\",\"event\":\"rollback\",\"round_id\":\"round-001\",\"reason\":\"seat-002 timed out\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-08T22:31:00.000Z\",\"rollback_event_id\":\"rollback-round-001-20260508T223100Z\",\"supersedes\":[\"seats/round-001/seat-001-cli-opencode.md\"]}\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/state-format.md:164:{\"schema_version\":\"1.2\",\"protocol\":\"ai-council\",\"producer\":\"persist-artifacts@1.2.0\",\"event\":\"artifact_superseded\",\"original_path\":\"seats/round-001/seat-001-cli-opencode.md\",\"round_id\":\"round-001\",\"rollback_event_id\":\"rollback-round-001-20260508T223100Z\",\"superseded_by\":\"rollback\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-08T22:31:00.000Z\"}\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/structure/state-format.md:224:- Agent body: `.opencode/agents/ai-council.md` §14\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v2.3.0.0.md:3:> Spec folder: `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/116-deep-skill-evolution/008-deep-skill-doc-evolution` (Level 2)\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.3.0.0.md:7:- Renamed the skill folder `.opencode/skills/sk-ai-council/` to `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-002-bare-command-halt.md:8:  \"entry_surface\": \"E2\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-002-bare-command-halt.md:12:  \"fixture\": \".opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-003-council-target\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-002-bare-command-halt.md:25:A pass halts without convening seats and surfaces a topic/setup prompt. Convening\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/scoring/scoring-rubric.md:217:- For a newly surfaced strength, allow a modest increase.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/scoring/scoring-rubric.md:303:Analytical Seat via cli-opencode\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/scoring/scoring-rubric.md:309:Analytical Seat, simulated cli-opencode lens\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/scoring/scoring-rubric.md:340:- Agent body: `.opencode/agents/ai-council.md` §6 SYNTHESIS PROTOCOL.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-001-auto-run-specified.md:8:  \"entry_surface\": \"E1\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-001-auto-run-specified.md:10:  \"prompt\": \"Convene a council to choose a rate-limit strategy for the slug API described in .opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-003-council-target/spec.md, then recommend one. :auto --packet=.opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-003-council-target --max-rounds=1\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/behavior-benchmark/scenarios/ACB-001-auto-run-specified.md:12:  \"fixture\": \".opencode/specs/deep-loops/033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks/fixtures/fx-003-council-target\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:3:description: \"Code-facing README for .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts.\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:19:This README documents the code-bearing folder `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts` so operators can understand its role without opening every source file first. It follows the sk-doc skill README structure while staying focused on code navigation.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:39:Start with `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md` for runtime routing and workflow boundaries.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:44:rg --files .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:60:| sk-code alignment | Points reviewers at OpenCode naming, header, error-handling, and type-discipline checks. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:81:| sk-code surface | OPENCODE | Applies OpenCode TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Shell, and config conventions. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:91:User request: Check .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts for sk-code and README coverage.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/README.md:112:| [`sk-code/SKILL.md`](../../../sk-code/SKILL.md) | OpenCode coding standards and verification routing. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v2.0.0.0.md:22:- Mirrored the runtime-agent contract across the OpenCode, Claude, and Codex agent surfaces.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:17:- `mode-registry.json` — every mode now carries the canon core fields: `packetKind: \"workflow\"`, `grandfatheredFolderMismatch: false` (folder == packetSkillName for all modes), and a well-formed `toolSurface` (all seven modes are mutating loop/host orchestrators; research additionally grants WebFetch for outward investigation). The three-tier discriminator and every `advisorRouting` projection block are unchanged.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:24:- `PARENT_HUB_CHECK_STRICT=1 parent-skill-check .opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows` — canon invariants pass (3d/3f/5/7a/8a).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:45:**Step 1: Invoke it.** The council offers two surfaces. Pick the one that fits your workload.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:51:python3 .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/skill_advisor.py \"run an ai council for the login refactor\" --threshold 0.8\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:74:node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs specs/042-pipeline \\\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:83:node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/advise-council-completion.cjs specs/042-pipeline\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:138:`behavior-benchmark/` (ACB scenarios) measures what an executor model actually does at the `/deep:ai-council` command surface under realistic vague/concise prompts: whether it convenes diverse seats (scored on **persisted seat artifacts**, since the common council is in-CLI with no task dispatch), how it presents, whether it stalls, and its latency versus a Claude baseline. Contracts + baselines live here; run evidence and the cross-mode scorecard live in the `033-deep-loop-behavior-benchmarks` packet.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:174:A: Two of three seats must agree on the material plan direction, and the critique pass must find no new high-severity blocker. If critique surfaces a blocker, the leading plan is not converged regardless of seat agreement. The rule prevents both false consensus and popularity contests.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:182:A: No. All seats inside one round must use the same CLI executor. Seat diversity within a round comes from different models or reasoning lenses on that CLI, not from mixing providers. If you want a different provider's vantage, add a second dedicated round. This keeps each round's sandbox, tool surface and output schema consistent.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:194:| README structure | `python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md --type readme` reports zero issues |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/README.md:195:| Skill package structure | `python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/quick_validate.py .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council` exits 0 |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v2.1.0.0.md:12:- Release-cleanup spec folder at `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/116-deep-skill-evolution/000-release-cleanup/004-deep-ai-council` with 4 JSON schemas and `resource-map.yaml`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:1:First release of `deep-ai-council` as a dedicated skill. Council deliberation moves out of `system-spec-kit` and into its own package, the runtime agent is renamed from `multi-ai-council` to `deep-ai-council` across all three runtimes, the advisor learns to route council prompts to the new skill, and the planning-only boundary is enforced through scoped-write helpers that only ever touch packet-local `ai-council/**` artifacts. Two spec packets ship behind this release: 101/001 created the skill surface, 101/003 expanded references and tests to fully document the agent contract.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:3:> Spec folders: `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/101-deep-multi-ai-council-skill/{001-deep-ai-council-skill-creation, 003-deep-ai-council-reference-expansion}` (Level 1 each)\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:15:The new `deep-ai-council` skill owns council activation triggers, smart routing across eight council intents, the planning-only operational boundary, and the rules that make council reports reproducible. The skill stays codebase-agnostic, so any project can dispatch a council without inheriting Webflow or OpenCode-specific patterns.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:21:The runtime agent now ships as `@deep-ai-council` across all three runtime mirrors (OpenCode, Claude, Codex). The agent body documents the 9-step workflow from RESOLVE through DELIVER, the dispatch depth rules (Depth 0 parallel via `Task`, Depth 1 sequential via `sequential_thinking` MCP), and the persistence protocol that calls writer functions in a fixed order so every artifact lands with an audit event.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:63:Six references cover the day-to-day surface: `output_schema.md` (the markdown report contract the parser enforces), `folder_layout.md` (packet-local artifact tree), `state_format.md` (append-only JSONL events), `command_wiring.md` (caller-owned post-dispatch persistence), `seat_diversity_patterns.md` (lens combinations and vantage targets), and `convergence_signals.md` (two-of-three-agree rule and escape hatches). Four further references were added in 101/003 to lift agent-body logic into the reference layer: `scoring_rubric.md` documents the 5-dimension rubric, multi-round deliberation, and the Hunter / Skeptic / Referee adversarial cross-critique; `depth_dispatch.md` codifies Depth 0 vs Depth 1 detection and no-recursive-counciling rules; `failure_handling.md` walks through timeouts, all-seats-fail, contradiction-without-resolution, and insufficient vantage diversity; `anti_patterns.md` lists the eleven council anti-patterns with detection cues and recovery actions.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:81:Targeted vitest coverage already exists at `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/multi-ai-council-*.vitest.ts` and continues to pass after the rename, the persistence library refactor, and the sk-code style alignment.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:97:No new top-level commands ship in this release. The agent is dispatched through normal Task delegation patterns, and the persistence helper at `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs` runs as a CLI wrapper for callers that need to persist a captured council report from outside the agent context.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:108:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md`                                   | Created — sk-doc template aligned, 8 numbered sections, 4-pattern smart router, 8-intent routing model   |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:109:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/README.md`                                  | Created — HVR style, 10 numbered sections, 252 lines                                                     |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:110:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/description.json`                           | Created — discovery metadata, version 1.0.0                                                              |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:111:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/graph-metadata.json`                        | Created — skill graph node, depends-on system-spec-kit, sibling deep-research                            |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:112:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/output-schema.md`                | Created — markdown report contract for the persistence parser                                            |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:113:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/folder-layout.md`                | Created — packet-local artifact tree                                                                     |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:114:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/state-format.md`                 | Created — append-only JSONL event semantics                                                              |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:115:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/command-wiring.md`               | Created — caller-owned post-dispatch persistence patterns                                                |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:116:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/seat-diversity-patterns.md`      | Created — Strategy lenses table, 5 diversity requirements, task-type auto-selection (264 lines)          |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:117:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/convergence-signals.md`          | Created — two-of-three-agree default, escape hatches, validator graduation note                          |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:118:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/scoring-rubric.md`               | Created — 5-dimension rubric, Hunter/Skeptic/Referee, conflict resolution matrix (343 lines)             |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:119:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/depth-dispatch.md`               | Created — Depth 0/1 detection, parallel/sequential, no-recursion (280 lines)                             |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:120:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/failure-handling.md`             | Created — timeouts, all-fail, contradiction, insufficient vantage (260 lines)                            |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:121:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/references/anti-patterns.md`                | Created — 11 council anti-patterns with detection cues and recovery actions (161 lines)                  |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:122:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs`              | Created — thin CLI wrapper delegating to lib                                                             |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:123:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/scripts/advise-council-completion.cjs`      | Created — completion advisory CLI for council artifact health checks                                     |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:124:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/persist-artifacts.js`           | Created — 7 named writers, scoped writes, parser, renderer, audit emission (760 lines)                   |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:125:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/audit-trail.js`                 | Created — JSONL state event normalization, artifact_written audit emission (143 lines)                   |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:126:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/rollback.js`                    | Created — round rollback move plus supersede event append (140 lines)                                   |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:127:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/package.json`                   | Created — `{ \"type\": \"commonjs\" }` boundary marker                                                       |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:128:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md` | Created — root playbook with 13 numbered sections, 18 scenarios indexed                            |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:129:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/01--runtime-routing-and-rename/`   | Created — DAC-001, DAC-002 (rename verification, advisor routing)                          |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:130:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/02--council-deliberation-and-seat-diversity/` | Created — DAC-003, DAC-004 (three-seat deliberation, cross-seat critique blocks premature convergence) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:131:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/03--artifact-persistence-and-state-format/` | Created — DAC-005, DAC-006, DAC-007 (helper writes packet tree, state JSONL records council_complete, schema strict-required sections fail-closed) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:132:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/04--convergence-and-rollback/` | Created — DAC-008, DAC-009, DAC-010 (two-of-three convergence, max-rounds non-converged, rollback forensics) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:133:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/05--scope-boundaries/` | Created — DAC-011, DAC-012 (graph exclusion, planning-only boundary)                                  |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:134:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/06--depth-and-failure-handling/` | Created — DAC-014, DAC-018 (depth detection, resume after interrupted state)                       |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:135:| `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/07--writer-library-contract/` | Created — DAC-013, DAC-015, DAC-016, DAC-017 (writer call sequence, 5-dim scoring application, Hunter/Skeptic/Referee critique, OUT_OF_SCOPE_WRITE rejection) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:136:| `.opencode/changelog/deep-ai-council`                                         | Created — symlink to `../skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/changelog`                                               |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:142:| `.opencode/agents/deep-ai-council.md`             | Created — `@deep-ai-council` definition, 19 numbered sections, scoped-write planning architect |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:150:| `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`                | Modified — explicit `deep-ai-council` council phrases bypass read-only guard     |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:151:| `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/scorer/native-scorer.vitest.ts`| Modified — added council prompt regression case                                  |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:169:If a downstream consumer still depends on the old runtime agent name, surface concrete evidence of the dependency before adding a compatibility shim — the project policy is to add shims only when a real consumer requires one.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:122:      \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:123:      \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:124:      \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:125:      \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:126:      \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:127:      \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/SKILL.md\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:128:      \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-alignment/SKILL.md\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:129:      \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/shared/synthesis/resource-map.cjs\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:130:      \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/README.md\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:136:        \"path\": \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:142:        \"path\": \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/graph-metadata.json:148:        \"path\": \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/README.md\",\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v2.0.0.0.md:19:- `.opencode/commands/deep/{research,review,ai-council}.md` — the 3 router one-liners invoking `render-command-contract.cjs` by hardcoded path, pulled forward from the planned reference-migration phase to close a sequencing gap (this phase's own live-verification step needs a working command surface).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v2.0.0.0.md:20:- ~29 additional self-referencing paths inside `deep-improvement/`'s own test suite (`model-benchmark/`, `shared/`, `agent-improvement/` test files) that named `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/` — simple workspace-root-anchored renames, unaffected by the depth change since `deep-improvement` itself didn't move deeper.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog/v2.0.0.0.md:26:- `/deep:*` command names, `@ai-council`/`@deep-research`/`@deep-review`/`@deep-improvement` agent names, and the remaining mode-packet folder names — all frozen. This is an identity-only rename; the public surface above the hub was deliberately not touched.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:3:description: \"Code-facing README for .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib.\"\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:19:This README documents the code-bearing folder `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib` so operators can understand its role without opening every source file first. It follows the sk-doc skill README structure while staying focused on code navigation.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:39:Start with `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md` for runtime routing and workflow boundaries.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:44:rg --files .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:60:| sk-code alignment | Points reviewers at OpenCode naming, header, error-handling, and type-discipline checks. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:80:| sk-code surface | OPENCODE | Applies OpenCode TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Shell, and config conventions. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:90:User request: Check .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib for sk-code and README coverage.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/lib/README.md:111:| [`sk-code/SKILL.md`](../../../../sk-code/SKILL.md) | OpenCode coding standards and verification routing. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:6:This prompt pack renders the per-iteration context for the `@deep-review` LEAF agent (native executor) or a CLI executor (e.g. `opencode run`). Tokens use curly-brace syntax and are substituted by `renderPromptPack` before dispatch.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:28:Load `.opencode/skills/sk-code/code-review/references/review-core.md` before final severity calls.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:5:Renamed the skill `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/` → `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/` and the agent `.opencode/agents/deep-ai-council.{md,toml}` → `.opencode/agents/ai-council.{md,toml}` across all three runtime mirrors. Family moved from `deep-loop` to `sk-util` per the parent spec.md §2 rationale: the Council is a planning sentinel skill (closer to sk-prompt's role) rather than an autonomous-loop executor like deep-research/deep-review which iterate to convergence. Behavior, trigger phrases, MCP wiring, council graph projection, and deliberation logic are all unchanged — this is a pure identity refactor.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:12:- Directory: `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/` → `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/` (via `git mv` — history preserved).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:14:  - `.opencode/agents/deep-ai-council.md` → `.opencode/agents/ai-council.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:20:| Surface group | Files |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:24:| Sibling skill graph edges | `cli-devin/graph-metadata.json`, `cli-opencode/graph-metadata.json` (already pointed at sk-* — unchanged); `deep-research/graph-metadata.json`, `deep-agent-improvement/graph-metadata.json`, `system-spec-kit/graph-metadata.json`, `system-skill-advisor/graph-metadata.json` (edges updated) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:27:| Council MCP test surface | `system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/multi-ai-council-runtime-parity.vitest.ts`, `council-helpers-smoke.vitest.ts`, `council-playbook-anchor-integrity.vitest.ts`, `multi-ai-council-audit-trail.vitest.ts`, `multi-ai-council-permission-scope.vitest.ts`, `multi-ai-council-rollback.vitest.ts`, `multi-ai-council-persist-artifacts.vitest.ts`, `scripts/test-council-matrix.sh` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:29:| Agent body skill-path references | each `ai-council.{md,toml}` body now references `Read(.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md)` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:32:| Skills index | `.opencode/skills/README.md` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:35:- Compiled `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/scripts/skill-graph.json` via `skill_graph_compiler.py --export-json --pretty`. Result: 22 skills, 6 families, `deep-ai-council` now appears in the `sk-util` family alongside `sk-prompt-small-model`, `sk-doc`, `sk-git`, `sk-prompt`, and `deep-agent-improvement`. `deep-loop` family is now strictly `deep-research` + `deep-review`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:38:- `.opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md` + `v1.1.0.0.md` — historical version state under the original name.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:39:- `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/101-deep-multi-ai-council-skill/**` (entire originating packet — 63 files documenting the work that created the skill).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:40:- `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/108-auto-review-quick-wins-verdict-markers-logging/**`, `110-auto-review-stretch-config-dedup-gates/**`, `113-cli-devin-prompt-quality/**` historical refs in past packets.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:49:| Live-surface rename | `rg \"deep-ai-council\"` on live allow-list | 0 hits |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:50:| Historical surfaces preserved | `git diff --stat` on 101/** + 108/** + 110/** + 113/** + sibling skill changelogs | unchanged |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:51:| Rename history | `git log --follow .opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-ai-council/SKILL.md` | traces back to original `deep-ai-council/SKILL.md` |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:54:| Advisor surfaces new name | `advisor_recommend({input: \"multi-seat AI Council deliberation\"})` | deep-ai-council at confidence **0.95** (above 0.7 threshold) |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:59:- `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/116-deep-skill-evolution/` (Phase 115 of skilled-agent-orchestration track, 6-phase decomposition: preflight + skill-rename + 4-runtime-agent-rename + cross-skill-edges-and-code + root-docs-hooks-and-readmes + reindex-validate-reconcile).\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:60:- Sister rename arc: `.opencode/specs/skilled-agent-orchestration/114-small-ai-model-optimization/007-sk-prompt-small-model-rename/` (sk-small-model → sk-prompt-small-model, shipped 2026-05-21) — established the mechanical-rename pattern that 115 reused.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:61:- Shared reference: `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/rename-pattern.md` — captures the reusable workflow for repo-wide rename refactors.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:28:When `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=1`, the directive shells out to `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub system-deep-loop --prompt \"<task>\"` before running the registry-driven routing above. The front door is a thin, promoted delegate: it resolves `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs` and calls `resolveRoute(hubId, taskText)`, which authorizes a compiled decision only when BOTH the tri-state runtime flag permits it AND `system-deep-loop`'s promoted activation manifest (`.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/010-live-activation/activation/system-deep-loop/manifest.json`) reports `servingAuthority: \"compiled\"`. Any other combination, or any error while resolving, prints the legacy sentinel and `system-deep-loop` routes unchanged. As of this writing, `system-deep-loop`'s promoted manifest already reports `servingAuthority: \"compiled\"` and `shadowOnly: false` — the tri-state flag is the sole gate currently withholding compiled serving by default.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:36:A served compiled decision returns one of four actions — `route` (use the returned `targets`), `clarify` or `defer` (disambiguate before proceeding), or `reject` (refuse) — which the `system-deep-loop` directive follows directly. The same decision, when returned inside `advisor_recommend`, is additionally attached to that recommendation's `compiledRoute` field and threaded into brief rendering as `metadata.compiledRouteSummary`; see [`advisor-recommend.md`](../../../system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/mcp-surface/advisor-recommend.md) for the shared advisor-side consumption path.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:40:`node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-status.cjs --hub system-deep-loop` reports `system-deep-loop`'s current serving posture as one stable JSON record with a `causeCode`: `compiled-serving` when the flag permits, the manifest authorizes, and the engine actually routes; `flag-off` or `legacy-authority` when the manifest is ready but the flag or manifest authority withholds it (expected drift, not breakage); `missing-manifest` when no promoted manifest exists; `engine-throw` when the flag and manifest both authorize compiled serving but the engine itself fails (a genuine break, distinct from expected drift). See [`feature-flag-governance.md`](../../../system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/governance/feature-flag-governance.md) for the `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING` flag-governance entry.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:50:| `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md` | Shared | Carries the opt-in compiled-routing directive `system-deep-loop` follows. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:51:| `.opencode/bin/compiled-route.cjs` | Script | Promoted CLI front door the directive shells out to. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:52:| `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/011-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs` | Shared | Tri-state flag parsing and the manifest serving-authority gate. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:53:| `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/010-live-activation/activation/system-deep-loop/manifest.json` | Shared | `system-deep-loop`'s promoted activation manifest (serving authority, shadow status, selected policy). |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:54:| `.opencode/bin/compiled-route-status.cjs` | Script | Per-hub serving-status probe with a drift-vs-break `causeCode`. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:60:| `.opencode/bin/compiled-routing-foundation.vitest.ts` | Automated test | Resolver, tri-state flag, and promoted-closure parity coverage. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:61:| `.opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/compiled-routing-consumption.vitest.ts` | Automated test | Advisor-side attach/consume/invalidate coverage shared by every eligible hub. |\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback/compiled-routing-and-legacy-fallback.md:74:- [advisor-recommend.md](../../../system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/mcp-surface/advisor-recommend.md) — how `advisor_recommend` attaches or omits `compiledRoute`.\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs:180:  // Council seats only ever spawn opencode/native subprocesses, so accepting cli-codex\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs:181:  // here silently ran a codex-labelled seat on opencode. Reject it explicitly and point\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs:185:      'cli-codex is not a supported AI Council seat executor (council seats run via opencode/native); use deep-review or deep-research for codex-backed loops',\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs:188:  if (!['native', 'cli-opencode', 'opencode'].includes(kind)) {\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs:191:  return kind === 'opencode' ? 'cli-opencode' : kind;\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs:229:function opencodeSeatArgs(model, seatPrompt) {\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs:258:    const child = spawnFn('opencode', opencodeSeatArgs(model, seatPrompt), {\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs:339:      command: 'opencode',\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/two-of-three-agree-triggers-convergence.md:49:1. `bash: sed -n '1,120p' .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md`\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/manual-testing-playbook/convergence-and-rollback/two-of-three-agree-trigge